    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-12932",
      "problem": "Suppose we have the events $A$ and $B$ with the following probabilities:\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.5,\\qquad P(B)=0.6,\\qquad P(A\\cap B)=0.3\n$$\n\nCalculate $P(A\\cup B).$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14275667/assets/35e807b7de787f50d0cbff770e4083cef84b4d35030b4c506b1db5646cf7a358.png)\n\nThe addition law for probability states that\n\n$$\nP(A\\cup B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A\\cap B).\n$$\n\nSo, to calculate $P(A\\cup B),$ we apply the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\  & =0.5+0.6-0.3 \\\\  & =0.8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe Venn diagram corresponding to this situation is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14275667/assets/8d2f63630f895af190b03f10f15af5bdaac35601201a601ec850e99325fc559d.png)",
